After some hassle, I managed to set it up.

I added newrelic as an external webpack dependency in nuxt.config.js
```javascript
    extend (config, ctx) {
      config.externals = [
        { newrelic: 'newrelic' }
      ]
    }
```

And then in nuxtServerInit I set the transaction name with code split so the bundle doesn't break in client side

```javascript
async nuxtServerInit ({ dispatch, commit }, context) {
    const newrelic = await import('newrelic')
    newrelic.setTransactionName(context.route.matched[0].path)
}
```

@nachogarcia Hey! I've configured my newrelic as same as you did and its working fine, but on the client interactions, Im having this error:

`logger.js?899e:6 Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: newrelic.noticeError is not a function`

Do you have any idea of wahts possibly going on? thanks ;)

I would take a look at how we handle in the Sentry module as inspiration: https://github.com/nuxt-community/sentry-module/blob/master/lib/module.js#L60-L73

To test easily without having to write a module, you can directly use hooks directly in your `nuxt.config.js`, example:

```js
export default {
  hooks: {
    'render:errorMiddleware'(app) {
      app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
        // Catch the error with you error reported
        console.error(`An error occured while rendering ${req.url}\n`, err)
        // Let Nuxt show the error page
        // You can customize the HTML error page for production by creating app/views/error.html
        next(err)
      })
    }
  }
}
```

@danielroe I tried the same setup, but I still get the same error `ReferenceError: newrelic is not defined` and noticed that the content of the script is `NREUM L(1)`
```
{
    hid: 'newrelic',
    innerHTML: '<!-- NREUM: (1) -->',
    type: 'text/javascript'
  }
```

I didn't create a plugin because on further inspection it might not be neccesary to set the names on each request, though in my system I have the configuration that was quoted above.

Since the change in configuration from some versions ago, you can just try to import newrelic in top of nuxt.config.js.

And if you need further customization, use a hook like

```
hooks: {
    'render:route' (url, result, context) {
      try {
        newrelic.setTransactionName(url)
      } catch (error) {
        // Ignore
      }
    }
  }
```

Please let me know what worked for you, so we can create a final and updated answer to anyone trying to setup newrelic with nuxt, and make a plugin if deemed neccesary :)
